1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,720
When you perform the initial installation of Burpsuite Enterprise Edition, you probably

2
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:14,800
chose to run the Enterprise web server and Enterprise server on the same machine that

3
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,180
you run scans on.

4
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:20,640
However, putting too many concurrent scans on the same scanning machine can cause performance

5
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,000
issues.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,920
In this case, you might want to deploy one or more dedicated scanning machines to ease

7
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:29,600
the load on your Enterprise server machine.

8
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:33,840
The setup process for a new scanning machine uses the same installer that you used for

9
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,360
the initial installation of Burpsuite Enterprise Edition.

10
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:40,760
However, you might need to download a different installer if your intended scanning machine

11
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:44,420
uses a different operating system.

12
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:50,260
On the machine you want to use, log into your account on porttwigga.net.

13
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:55,160
Under your licenses and products, download the installer for the same version of Burpsuite

14
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:58,320
Enterprise Edition that is installed on your Enterprise server machine.

15
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:01,720
This is also available from our downloads page.

16
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:05,720
Open the installer and follow the same process that you did when installing Burpsuite Enterprise

17
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,180
Edition.

18
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:12,440
When asked what you want to use the machine for, deselect running the Enterprise web server,

19
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:16,560
and Enterprise server, and select running scans.

20
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:21,340
When prompted, enter the hostname or IP address of the machine where you previously installed

21
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:23,320
the Enterprise server.

22
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:29,000
External scanning machines automatically access the Enterprise server on port 8072.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,840
When the installation is complete, you are given a fingerprint of the scanning machine's

24
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:34,960
public key.

25
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:40,360
You need to keep this to authorize the new scanning machine later.

26
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:45,760
Log into the web UI as an administrator and go to the scanning machine settings page.

27
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:50,460
On the authorization request tab, you should see a pending authorization request showing

28
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:52,760
the IP address of the new scanning machine.

29
00:01:52,760 --> 00:02:07,160
If you are using a standard deployment, as opposed to a Kubernetes deployment, choose the pool that

30
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:09,160
the scanning machine will belong to.

31
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:13,600
Compare the public key fingerprint shown with the one that you saved after setting up the

32
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:14,600
new scanning machine.

33
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:17,820
If they match, click authorize.

34
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:22,060
The scanning machine is now available for use on the scanning machine settings page and

35
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:23,560
you can start assigning scans to it.

